{"cantica":"purgatorio","cantoNumber":25,"title":"Canto XXV","totalDuration":344.015,"segments":[{"id":1,"speaker":"narrator","text":"Now nothing could delay our upward climb—\nthe sun had left its midday circle in Taurus,\nand night had claimed Scorpio's domain.\nSo like a man who never hesitates\nbut walks his path no matter what appears,\nwhen necessity's sharp spur drives him forward,\nwe entered through that narrow cleft,\nclimbing the stairway single file,\nits tightness forcing climbers apart.\nAnd like a young stork lifting its wing\nwith longing to take flight, yet lacking courage\nto leave the nest, letting the wing fall back—\nso was I, with my desire to ask\nkindled then quenched, making those movements\nof one preparing to speak.\nDespite our rapid pace,\nmy gentle father did not hold back, but said:","startTime":0,"endTime":43.76,"words":[{"word":"Now","start":0.16,"end":0.56},{"word":"nothing","start":0.56,"end":1.04},{"word":"could","start":1.04,"end":1.28},{"word":"delay","start":1.28,"end":1.52},{"word":"our","start":1.52,"end":1.68},{"word":"upward","start":1.68,"end":2.08},{"word":"climb—","start":2.08,"end":3.12},{"word":"the","start":3.12,"end":3.28},{"word":"sun","start":3.28,"end":3.6},{"word":"had","start":3.6,"end":3.88},{"word":"left","start":3.88,"end":4.08},{"word":"its","start":4.08,"end":4.24},{"word":"midday","start":4.24,"end":4.72},{"word":"circle","start":4.72,"end":5.12},{"word":"in","start":5.12,"end":5.24},{"word":"Taurus,","start":5.24,"end":6.12},{"word":"and","start":6.12,"end":6.4},{"word":"night","start":6.4,"end":6.64},{"word":"had","start":6.64,"end":6.8},{"word":"claimed","start":6.8,"end":7.2},{"word":"Scorpio's","start":7.2,"end":7.84},{"word":"domain.","start":7.84,"end":9.04},{"word":"So","start":9.04,"end":9.28},{"word":"like","start":9.28,"end":9.44},{"word":"a","start":9.44,"end":9.6},{"word":"man","start":9.6,"end":9.96},{"word":"who","start":9.96,"end":10.16},{"word":"never","start":10.16,"end":10.48},{"word":"h